.TH "CSDLC-FINISH" "1" "September 11, 2026" "C-SDLC v3" "ADL Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
csdlc\-finish \- reconcile terminal issue truth
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&csdlc finish ISSUE [\-\-disposition DISPOSITION.json] [\-\-preview plan]
.fi
.nf
\&csdlc finish \-\-request REQUEST [\-\-observe\-github]
\&csdlc finish \-\-help
.fi
.SH ISSUE INTENT FORM
\&The #869 issue intent forms are a candidate contract, pending the required exact\-head validation/review and separate installation/activation. They do not replace the active operator binary. Existing \-\-request forms below retain their existing native contracts. See docs/csdlc\-v3/INTENT_COMMANDS.md for complete strict content and effect boundaries.
.PP
\&The intent form derives canonical PR identity and authenticates merged PR plus closed issue through the existing terminal owner. Successful execution retains terminal state and receipt in primary Git metadata. \-\-preview plan observes without persistence. It does not merge or close the issue itself.
.PP
\&Optional \-\-repo\-root selects discovery, \-\-json retains machine output, and \-\-emit\-request returns a generated wrapper accepted directly by COMMAND \-\-intent\-request REQUEST.json; its inner request is also accepted. Both forms share identity and mutation guards.
.PP
\&Optional \-\-disposition supplies strict disposition/operator/rationale/evidence_refs for native no\-PR terminal reconciliation. Disposition uses retired_without_execution, duplicate, superseded, absorbed, coordination_completed or historical_disposition. The adapter authenticates closed issue timestamps internally and the native owner rechecks them before persistence; no caller timestamps or internal receipts are required. Administrative disposition is not merged implementation proof.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&The following details describe the retained request\-based form. The candidate issue intent form is specified above.
.PP
\&Requires authenticated GitHub observation of a merged PR with the exact expected head, closing linkage and closed issue. mode must be closing; part_of checkpoints cannot finish. \-\-observe\-github is necessary for public authenticated finish; caller\-authored public_adapter_receipt is not trusted. terminal_state is optional: omit to observe, include canonical output paths to retain terminal state and receipt. Finish does not merge or close GitHub issues.
.SH OPTIONS
\&The following details describe the retained request\-based form. The candidate issue intent form is specified above.
.PP
\&\-\-request: Required path to a UTF\-8 JSON request of the command's request family.
.PP
\&\-\-observe\-github: Perform authenticated GitHub readback. Requires selected credentials. It does not itself create, update or merge a PR.
.PP
\&\-\-help: Show standalone help; \-h is equivalent.
.PP
\&\-h: Show standalone help; do not combine with execution options.
.SH REQUEST
\&The following details describe the retained request\-based form. The candidate issue intent form is specified above.
.PP
\&TerminalRouteRequest, with only the relevant finish, cleanup or cutover fields. See csdlc\-requests(1). Examples under docs/csdlc\-v3/man/examples use fixture identities and are not permission to mutate those targets.
.SH EFFECTS
\&The following details describe the retained request\-based form. The candidate issue intent form is specified above.
.PP
\&Authenticated readback plus optional local terminal persistence; no GitHub write. A successful terminal observation without terminal_state does not create a durable terminal receipt.
.SH FILES
\&The following details describe the retained request\-based form. The candidate issue intent form is specified above.
.PP
\&Primary terminal paths: resolved Git metadata csdlc\-v3/local/v3/issues/ISSUE/terminal.json and csdlc\-v3/local/evidence/ISSUE/terminal\-receipt.json. Linked paths: .csdlc/v3/issues/ISSUE/terminal.json and .csdlc/evidence/ISSUE/terminal\-receipt.json. Request terminal_state.repository_root must be the real reconciliation checkout; state_path and receipt_path must resolve exactly to those locations.
.SH EXAMPLES
\&The following details describe the retained request\-based form. The candidate issue intent form is specified above.
.nf
\&csdlc finish \-\-request finish\-request.json \-\-observe\-github
.fi
.PP
\&Use csdlc\-workflow(1) for ordered finish and cleanup; cutover/rollback examples validate the schema and denial boundary, not a new transition authorization.
.SH RECOVERY
\&The following details describe the retained request\-based form. The candidate issue intent form is specified above.
.PP
\&Retain original evidence and exact current checkout identity. Stale terminal state requires a matching expected_state_digest; mismatched receipt identity must be investigated, never overwritten. Refresh a clean preview after any target/head/registration change. Unsupported or unproven transition states fail closed; do not fall back to deleted wrappers.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&csdlc(1), csdlc\-requests(1), csdlc\-workflow(1).
